# Eton Manor AC — Proposed Site Structure & Navigation

Based on a full review of the exported content (`content/`, 95 archived pages from the 111-URL
sitemap). This proposes a new information architecture to replace the current one, which grew
organically over ~10 years of ad-hoc page creation.

## Key findings

1. **78% of published pages are unreachable from the main navigation.** The live nav has only 4
   top-level items with dropdowns (The Club, About Us, Membership, Event Reports) covering 21
   pages. The other 74 — Training, Racing, Results, Grand Prix, Social, Shop, Teams, Contact, Club
   Calendar, and more — exist only as direct URLs with no menu path to them.

2. **The same seasonal content is republished under a new URL every season instead of one
   structured archive.** Race results alone span 12 separate top-level pages with inconsistent,
   non-chronological slugs: `results`, `results-2`, `results-3`, `results-4`,
   `results-current-season`, `summer-season-2017/2018/2019`, `summer-season-2021-results`,
   `winter-season-2017-18`, `winter-season-2019-20`, `2018-19-winter-results`. Because of this,
   `results-current-season` is actually **two seasons out of date** — `results-4` (Winter 2023/24)
   is the real current one. Grand Prix tables have the same problem across 12 pages
   (`eton-manor-ac-grand-prix-tables` + 11 dated `grand-prix-YYYY-season` pages), though at least
   those use a consistent, sortable slug — that pattern should be the template for Results too.

3. **Two parallel news systems exist.** A real dated blog (`/YYYY/MM/DD/slug/`, e.g.
   `2023/11/12/north-london-xc-hosted-by-eton-manor/`) sits alongside a static "Event Reports"
   nav section (`news-2/` + 6 standalone pages) covering the same kind of content — and at least
   one topic (Autumn Marathons 2021) appears to have been published in **both** systems under
   near-identical slugs.

4. **Dead and duplicate pages are still published:**
   - `about-the-club/` — empty page, superseded by `about-us/` (which the nav actually uses).
   - `join-the-club/` (top-level) — empty; the real membership application form lives at
     `join/join-the-club/`.
   - `contact-us/` vs `contact-us-2/` — two different contact implementations (an AJAX form vs. a
     static list of mailto links). Only one should remain.
   - `shop/` vs `shop-2/` — a dynamic (WooCommerce) shop and a static one. Same call.
   - `teams/second-team/` and `teams/another-team/` — literal placeholder/test entries in the
     internal fixtures database, still publicly live.

5. **The `/join/` membership form leaks the full member roster** to anonymous visitors via a
   hidden admin field (reported separately — see `README.md`). Any rebuilt Join flow must not
   reintroduce this.

6. **`/teams/*` isn't really public content.** It's the internal opponent/fixtures database
   (GravityView), showing "no entries match your request" to anyone not logged in as a matching
   member. It doesn't belong in public navigation at all.

## Proposed navigation (top level)

```
About          Training        Racing          Social         News          Membership       Shop      Contact
```

8 top-level items, each a real landing page with working links to its children (the current
`the-club/`, `racing/`, `social/` pages describe their sub-areas in prose but link to none of
them — every proposed landing page should fix that).

